---A rotation: `Quat()` is the identity and `Quat(x, y, z, w)` is normalized. `a * b` applies b, then
---a; `q * v` rotates a vector. Angles are in degrees.
---@class Quat
---@overload fun(): Quat
---@overload fun(x: number, y: number, z: number, w: number): Quat
---@field x number
---@field y number
---@field z number
---@field w number
---@operator mul(Quat): Quat
---@operator mul(Vec3): Vec3
Quat = {}

---Euler angles in degrees: (pitch, yaw, roll).
---@return Vec3
function Quat:euler() end

---@return Quat
function Quat:inverse() end

---@return Quat
function Quat:normalized() end

---The rotated forward direction (-Z).
---@return Vec3
function Quat:forward() end

---The rotated right direction (+X).
---@return Vec3
function Quat:right() end

---The rotated up direction (+Y).
---@return Vec3
function Quat:up() end

---Spherical interpolation: t = 0 gives this rotation, t = 1 gives other.
---@param other Quat
---@param t number
---@return Quat
function Quat:slerp(other, t) end

---@return Quat
function Quat.identity() end

---A rotation from Euler angles in degrees.
---@param pitch number
---@param yaw number
---@param roll number
---@return Quat
---@overload fun(degrees: Vec3): Quat
function Quat.fromEuler(pitch, yaw, roll) end

---A rotation of `degrees` around an axis.
---@param axis Vec3
---@param degrees number
---@return Quat
function Quat.axisAngle(axis, degrees) end

---The rotation that looks along a direction (its forward, -Z, becomes direction).
---@param direction Vec3
---@param up? Vec3 Defaults to +Y.
---@return Quat
function Quat.lookRotation(direction, up) end

---The shortest rotation that turns one direction into another.
---@param from Vec3
---@param to Vec3
---@return Quat
function Quat.fromTo(from, to) end

